@nsobid-41EAE379C103E9A512CFA931BA400E938B3B7C55

# Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables both of the game's anti-aliasing methods.
//
// The StressParam AntiAliasingType chooses between them each frame. Type 0 runs
// agl::pfx::FilterAA (FXAA, ReduceAA, SMAA or a callback, by its
// antialias_type) at the end of al::ViewRenderer::drawView, and falls back to
// pseudo AA when the FXAA alpha-out parameter is zero. Type 2 is pseudo AA:
// al::GraphicsStressDirector::movement alternates a sub-pixel projection
// offset (0, then 0.25 over the buffer size) every frame and drawView adds it
// to the camera, so edges average out over two frames. Type 1 uses neither.
//
// al::GraphicsSystemInfo::preDrawGraphics rewrites FilterAA's enable flag every
// frame from that choice. It now always stores false, so drawView takes its own
// no-filter path regardless of the type or any FilterAA parameter. drawView's
// check for pseudo AA now branches straight past the offset, so the camera
// stays put. The result is the image type 1 produces.

@enabled
002DBE6C 1F2003D5   // NOP: FilterAA enable is always stored as false (was CBZ W8 on AntiAliasingType == 0)
002DE86C 14000014   // B past the pseudo AA projection offset (was CMP W8,#2 on AntiAliasingType)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Captain Toad Treasure Tracker 1.4.2 (al +
// agl + sead, NVN). The retail build keeps its symbol table; every site was
// located by symbol and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
